...that usually makes me great.

263
00:16:10,210 --> 00:16:12,340
So I had to do all this other stuff.

264
00:16:12,550 --> 00:16:15,590
And the response I got! Man, oh, man.

265
00:16:15,800 --> 00:16:17,970
It was like a ticker-tape parade!

266
00:16:20,020 --> 00:16:23,560
Yes I know. As it happens, my room is very close to the parade route.

267
00:16:29,360 --> 00:16:33,030
It was amazing, and not just for her. Uh-uh. For me too.

268
00:16:33,240 --> 00:16:36,320
It's like, all of a sudden, I'm blind...

269
00:16:36,530 --> 00:16:38,700
...but all my other senses are heightened.

270
00:16:38,910 --> 00:16:42,540
You know? It's like, I was able to appreciate it...

271
00:16:42,750 --> 00:16:44,790
...on another level.

272
00:16:47,420 --> 00:16:49,840
I didn't know you had another level.

273
00:16:50,380 --> 00:16:52,170
I know. Neither did I!

274
00:17:01,680 --> 00:17:03,930
Hey, great skirts!Birthday present?

275
00:17:04,140 --> 00:17:05,730
from who?

276
00:17:04,140 --> 00:17:05,730
 from you.

277
00:17:05,940 --> 00:17:08,060
I exchanged the blouse you got me.

278
00:17:09,770 --> 00:17:11,360
Well, it's the thought.

279
00:17:12,190 --> 00:17:14,690
Doesn't Ross' flight get in in a couple hours?

280
00:17:14,950 --> 00:17:16,740
At gate 27B?

281
00:17:18,160 --> 00:17:19,870
Uh, yeah.

282
00:17:20,080 --> 00:17:22,540
Monica, you know, I've been thinking about it.

283
00:17:22,750 --> 00:17:26,120
I've decided this Ross thing is not a good idea.

284
00:17:26,330 --> 00:17:28,170
Why?

285
00:17:26,330 --> 00:17:28,170
Because I feel...

286
00:17:28,380 --> 00:17:30,920
...like I wouldn't just be going out with him.

287
00:17:31,130 --> 00:17:33,210
I would be going out with all of you.

288
00:17:33,420 --> 00:17:37,010
Ugh, there'd be all this pressure and...

289
00:17:33,420 --> 00:17:37,010
No pressure, no pressure!

290
00:17:38,800 --> 00:17:41,800
Nothing has even happened yet and you're already so...

291
00:17:42,010 --> 00:17:43,350
I'm not "so."

292
00:17:43,560 --> 00:17:45,770
I was a teensy bit weird at first...

293
00:17:45,980 --> 00:17:48,850
...but I'll be good. I promise.

294
00:17:54,110 --> 00:17:55,150
Who is it?

295
00:17:55,360 --> 00:17:56,690
It's me, Carl.

296
00:17:56,900 --> 00:17:57,990
Come on up.

297
00:17:58,200 --> 00:17:59,950
Behind my brother's back?

298
00:18:01,530 --> 00:18:05,840
Is the kind of crazy thing you won't be hearing from me.

299
00:18:18,840 --> 00:18:22,140
Seven hundred bucks.

300
00:18:18,840 --> 00:18:22,140
All right, you Did it.

301
00:18:22,350 --> 00:18:23,720
Do we have any fruit?

302
00:18:26,850 --> 00:18:28,810
Man, hell of a two weeks, huh?

303
00:18:29,020 --> 00:18:32,020
You know what, though? I really feel I learned something.

304
00:18:32,230 --> 00:18:34,860
So you'll stick with this "it's all for her" thing?

305
00:18:35,070 --> 00:18:36,860
What, are you crazy?

306
00:18:37,070 --> 00:18:41,450
When a blind man gets his sight back, does he walk around like this?

307
00:18:46,910 --> 00:18:50,290
I'm just saying, if I see one more picture of Ed Begley Jr...

308
00:18:50,500 --> 00:18:52,540
...in that stupid electric car...

309
00:18:52,750 --> 00:18:54,250
...I'm gonna shoot myself!

310
00:18:56,460 --> 00:19:00,220
Don't get me wrong. I'm not against environmental issues, per se...

311
00:19:00,430 --> 00:19:02,180
...it's just that guy!

312
00:19:02,390 --> 00:19:06,600
I can't believe you'd rather go out with him than me.

313
00:19:06,810 --> 00:19:10,020
Excuse me, please. I'm trying to have a date here.

314
00:19:10,230 --> 00:19:13,190
Fine, just stop thinking about me.

315
00:19:16,190 --> 00:19:18,400
Can't do it, can you?

316
00:19:19,240 --> 00:19:21,530
So I'm thinking about you. So what?

317
00:19:21,820 --> 00:19:24,950
I don't get it. What do you see in this guy anyway?

318
00:19:25,160 --> 00:19:28,540
Well, he seems to be a very nice guy.

319
00:19:28,750 --> 00:19:32,470
I mean, come on, buddy! Get a real car!

320
00:19:35,090 --> 00:19:38,590
Rachel, come on. Give us a chance.

321
00:19:39,340 --> 00:19:41,220
Ross, it's too hard.

322
00:19:39,340 --> 00:19:41,220
No, no.

323
00:19:41,430 --> 00:19:43,340
Because it'll get weird for everyone else?

324
00:19:43,550 --> 00:19:45,720
Who cares about them? This is about us.

325
00:19:45,930 --> 00:19:49,430
I've been in love with you since the ninth grade.

326
00:19:49,640 --> 00:19:52,190
You're, like, my best friend.

327
00:19:49,640 --> 00:19:52,190
I know.

328
00:19:52,390 --> 00:19:54,350
If We broke up, and I lost you...

329
00:19:54,560 --> 00:19:56,400
Why do you think we'll break up?

330
00:19:56,610 --> 00:20:00,480
Have you been involved with someone where you haven't broken up?

331
